{"id":"[REDACTED]","object":"chat.completion","created":1790942304,"model":"mercury-2","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"record_type\": \"reduction\",\n  \"summary\": \"The audit examined all 11 changed targets and associated source/diff units (total of 1246 lines in run‑ledger.js and 1409 lines in adversarial‑review.js). Most modules were found to have no concrete defects (ask.js, codex‑challenger.js, llm‑client.js, consensus.js, reviewer‑panel.js, doctrine‑review.js, etc.). Notable issues include two silent‑default patterns (flagFromEnv in adversarial‑review.js and optionalEnvBoolean in config.js) that mask mis‑configurations, and the removal of the Opus fallback in provider‑preflight.js which reduces provider coverage. Eight fourth‑shape additions (throws, guards, and fallback changes) were detected in adversarial‑review.js and config.js. Several units remain unresolved due to malformed shard attempts or missing provider records (adversarial‑review.js diff, run‑ledger.js fragment, consensus.permissionMode reference search). Incomplete AST fragments prevent assessment of error‑handling mechanisms. Live shard gaps list outstanding unit IDs. Overall evidence is comprehensive but includes unresolved and malformed portions.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"F001\",\n      \"target\": \"trai_brain/mercury-bridge/adversarial-review.js\",\n      \"category\": \"MECHANICAL\",\n      \"basis\": \"RECEIPT\",\n      \"summary\": \"flagFromEnv silently returns false for any unrecognised environment variable value without emitting a warning, potentially masking configuration errors.\",\n      \"citations\": [\n        \"trai_brain/mercury-bridge/adversarial-review.js:122-129\"\n      ],\n      \"status\": \"examined\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"F002\",\n      \"target\": \"trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js\",\n      \"category\": \"MECHANICAL\",\n      \"basis\": \"RECEIPT\",\n      \"summary\": \"optionalEnvBoolean returns false for any env value not matching known true/false strings, providing a silent default that can hide mis‑configuration.\",\n      \"citations\": [\n        \"trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js:81-87\"\n      ],\n      \"status\": \"examined\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"F003\",\n      \"target\": \"trai_brain/mercury-bridge/provider-preflight.js\",\n      \"category\": \"SUBSTANTIVE\",\n      \"basis\": \"RECEIPT\",\n      \"summary\": \"Fallback to Opus when the Fable client fails was removed, reducing provider coverage and possibly causing pre‑flight checks to fail where the Opus fallback would have succeeded.\",\n      \"citations\": [\n        \"trai_brain/mercury-bridge/provider-preflight.js:232-246\"\n      ],\n      \"status\": \"examined\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"F004\",\n      \"target\": \"adversarial-review.js & config.js\",\n      \"category\": \"MECHANICAL\",\n      \"basis\": \"RECEIPT\",\n      \"summary\": \"Eight fourth‑shape additions (throws, guards, and fallback changes) were introduced: throw new Error('Kimi final adjudication prompt requires the Astra review object') at line 805, boundary‑error handling at line 1237, and multiple consensus‑related throws in config.js lines 473‑488.\",\n      \"citations\": [\n        \"trai_brain/mercury-bridge/adversarial-review.js:805\",\n        \"trai_brain/mercury-bridge/adversarial-review.js:1237\",\n        \"trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js:473-488\"\n      ],\n      \"status\": \"examined\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"U001\",\n      \"target\": \"trai_brain/mercury-bridge/adversarial-review.js (diff)\",\n      \"category\": \"SUBSTANTIVE\",\n      \"basis\": \"RECEIPT\",\n      \"summary\": \"Exported function name changed from runFableAdversarialReview to runAstraAdversarialReview and fallback handling for Opus and Fable was removed; impact uncertain due to lack of evidence of remaining imports.\",\n      \"citations\": [\n        \"trai